# SIMF — .gitignore

# ── Production secrets — NEVER commit real values (SIMF-OPS-001 §6) ──
# deploy/set-env.template.ps1 is the tracked template: every Secret entry is
# empty and a test enforces it. deploy/set-env.ps1 is the FILLED overlay an
# operator creates on the server — real connection strings, SMTP password and
# keys — and must stay untracked. Never delete that rule to "share" the script.
# deploy/set-env-api.ps1 is the pre-2026-08-06 filled overlay, still ignored so
# an existing server's copy cannot be committed by accident.
set-env-prod.ps1
set-env-*.local.ps1
deploy/set-env.ps1
deploy/set-env-api.ps1

# ── Runtime file store — personal data, NEVER commit ───────────────
# App_Data/files is the filesystem storage root (FilesystemFileStorageProvider),
# so anything a local run uploads lands here: avatars, ID-document scans,
# speaker photos. 55 such files had been committed by accident and were
# untracked on 2026-08-05; they are runtime artifacts, referenced by nothing in
# source, and an ID scan has no business in source control. Ignored so a
# `git add` on the project directory cannot sweep them back in.
src/Backend/SIMF.Api/App_Data/files/
src/Backend/SIMF.Api/App_Data/recordings/

# ── .NET build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
artifacts/
publish/
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb

# ── Visual Studio / Rider ──────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# ── Flutter / Dart ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
*.iml
src/MobileApp/build/
Pods/
.gradle/
local.properties
# Golden-comparison output. `flutter test` writes the four diff PNGs per failing
# golden here; they are generated artefacts of a FAILING run, never an input to
# one. 48 of them had been committed and were stale against a long-superseded
# revision, so anyone grepping the directory was reading obsolete debris
# (STALE-GOLDEN-ARTIFACTS). The masters live in test/golden/goldens/.
src/Mobile/simf_app/test/golden/failures/

# ── Secrets & environment ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Production config is applied via Machine-scope env vars (set-env-*.ps1);
# real secret values are NEVER committed. Only the placeholder template is.
appsettings.Production.json
appsettings.*.Local.json
*.env
.env
secrets.json
set-env-*.local.ps1

# ── Claude Code local settings ─────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Logs & temp ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime log output only — root-anchored so source-tree `Logs/` folders
# (e.g. SIMF.Application/Logs, SIMF.Api/Endpoints/Admin/Logs) stay tracked.
*.log
/logs/
*.tmp

# ── UI-audit scratch (generated screenshots, run logs, helper scripts) ─
/.ui-audit/

# ── OS files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Repo-root scratch notes. txt.txt was tracked and carried a plaintext
# production super-admin credential (twice) plus demo passwords; removed
# 2026-07-30. Scratch files do not belong in the repo at all.
txt.txt
# SEC-NOTES (2026-07-30) — myComment.txt is the owner's hand-written fix-list.
# Untracked, NOT deleted: it is owner-authored, other work still references it,
# and it stays on disk. Untracked because a plaintext working-notes file at the
# repo root has no review gate — the next paste into it lands in a commit with
# nobody reading it, which is how txt.txt came to carry a production credential.
# Requires `git rm --cached myComment.txt` once, or the tracked copy survives
# this ignore rule.
myComment.txt
/*.scratch.txt

# Test run artefacts. A .trx captures the whole test console log; two of
# these were tracked at 707 MB and 564 MB, so every clone paid 1.2 GB for
# stale output. Nothing reads them.
TestResults/
*.trx
